00:09:26.529 --> 00:09:27.864
- That's right.
- And it went (boing).

00:09:27.864 --> 00:09:29.347
(speaks indistinctly)
(Chuck buzzes lips)

00:09:29.347 --> 00:09:31.460
And they're identical to each
other except they're speaking

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:33.390
each other's languages.
- Each other languages, right.

00:09:33.390 --> 00:09:35.890
- Which by the way is almost as believable

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:37.130
as the Tower of Babel.

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:37.963
Anyway, go ahead.

00:09:37.963 --> 00:09:40.194
- The reason I did not cringe at that one

00:09:40.194 --> 00:09:41.230
is because--
- Wait, wait, wait.

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:43.680
What fraction of our audience
even have seen that movie?

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:44.909
- Well, you didn't ask me that question.

00:09:44.909 --> 00:09:46.637
- You gotta be like 80 years
old to have seen that movie.

00:09:46.637 --> 00:09:49.750
No, I know that on college campuses,

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:52.490
many college campuses,
there's the annual watching

00:09:52.490 --> 00:09:54.470
of the Batman movie.
- [Tyson] Gotcha.

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:55.534
- Holy AARP Batman!

00:09:55.534 --> 00:09:58.701
(hysterical laughter)

00:10:00.770 --> 00:10:01.603
- Okay.

00:10:01.603 --> 00:10:03.517
- Wheel me closer to
the screen. (laughing)

00:10:03.517 --> 00:10:06.280
- Robin, I do believe
that man stole my walker.

00:10:06.280 --> 00:10:11.280
- Wait, so Mike, my cringing was, okay.

00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:14.840
I even allowed there to
have been shark repellent

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:15.673
in a spray can.
- [Liu] Yes.

00:10:15.673 --> 00:10:16.506
- Okay, this is pre--

00:10:16.506 --> 00:10:17.857
- But there was Bat Manta
Repellent and there was

00:10:17.857 --> 00:10:20.770
Bat Eel Repellent, whatever it was.

00:10:20.770 --> 00:10:22.210
- Here's my thing.

00:10:22.210 --> 00:10:27.080
My issue was, how big is his utility belt

00:10:27.950 --> 00:10:30.750
to just always happen
to have shark repellent?

00:10:30.750 --> 00:10:32.880
- He didn't have the bat shark repellent

00:10:32.880 --> 00:10:34.840
on him at that time.

00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:36.250
It was in the vehicle.

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:37.750
It was in the Bat-copter.

00:10:37.750 --> 00:10:41.310
And the shark was attached to Batman's leg

00:10:41.310 --> 00:10:43.380
as he was coming up on the rope ladder

00:10:43.380 --> 00:10:44.570
and he said, "Quick Robin,

00:10:44.570 --> 00:10:46.552
hand me the Bat Shark Repellent"

00:10:46.552 --> 00:10:48.470
(laughing)
And so, from the cabinet

00:10:48.470 --> 00:10:49.713
that had the Bat Shark Repellent,

00:10:49.713 --> 00:10:52.050
that manta ray repellent,
that whatever repellent.

00:10:52.050 --> 00:10:53.968
- A repellent for each
kind of bad aquatic--

00:10:53.968 --> 00:10:54.801
- Yeah.

00:10:54.801 --> 00:10:56.930
- It's like a spice rack of repellents.

00:10:56.930 --> 00:10:58.600
- And he grabbed the
thing and then sprayed it

00:10:58.600 --> 00:11:00.730
and then it fell down and it exploded.

00:11:00.730 --> 00:11:02.590
- Okay, I thought it came
from his utility belt.

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:03.423
Okay, so now explain.

00:11:03.423 --> 00:11:06.160
- So, the reason it wasn't
cringe worthy for me

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:10.900
is because I knew it was
totally goofy to begin with.

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:12.970
- [Tyson] Campy, right, okay.
- And in a sense,

00:11:12.970 --> 00:11:16.320
I prefer movies of that genre,

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:18.280
that don't take themselves too seriously.

00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:19.150
- Like Mars Attacks.

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:20.030
- Yes, if they're obviously messed up,

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:21.790
- Well, there you go.

00:11:21.790 --> 00:11:22.623
- Then I don't really
worry too much about--

00:11:22.623 --> 00:11:23.630
- Ack ack.

00:11:23.630 --> 00:11:25.940
- What bothers me, yeah.

00:11:25.940 --> 00:11:26.860
- That's Mars Attacks, I'm sorry.

00:11:26.860 --> 00:11:27.693
- Was that really?

00:11:27.693 --> 00:11:28.913
- That's my Mars Attacks. (imitates alien)

00:11:28.913 --> 00:11:30.620
- Yeah, the aliens say, "Ack ack."

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:31.839
- Ack ack.

00:11:31.839 --> 00:11:32.672
- And they were destroyed only by--

00:11:32.672 --> 00:11:34.540
Ope, should we spoil the movie?

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:36.960
- I don't know if you should do that.

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:38.120
- No, lets not spoil the movie.

00:11:38.120 --> 00:11:39.100
But it turns out--

00:11:39.100 --> 00:11:40.570
- You're worried about
spoiling Mars Attacks?

00:11:40.570 --> 00:11:42.977
- Yeah, something completely
unexpected saves the world.

00:11:42.977 --> 00:11:45.940
- Now the kids have
something to go look at.

00:11:45.940 --> 00:11:46.773
Go look at it kids!

00:11:46.773 --> 00:11:51.100
- So, in that vein, my
movie where I just said,

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:52.839
okay I'm leaving all the reality--

00:11:52.839 --> 00:11:54.483
- [Liu] Reality behind,
and no matter what--

00:11:54.483 --> 00:11:55.530
- [Nice] Suspending all disbelief.

00:11:55.530 --> 00:11:56.780
- Attack of the Killer Tomatoes.

00:11:56.780 --> 00:11:57.613
- Yes!

00:11:57.613 --> 00:12:00.016
- [Everyone] (singing) Attack
of the killing tomatoes!

00:12:01.129 --> 00:12:03.874
- So the tomato is just
jumping and smothering people.

00:12:03.874 --> 00:12:04.707
- [Liu] Yes! (laughs)

00:12:04.707 --> 00:12:06.049
- And I said, "Okay."

00:12:06.049 --> 00:12:08.224
- Oh my God, I'm dying by deliciousness!

00:12:08.224 --> 00:12:09.057
(laughing)

00:12:09.057 --> 00:12:11.540
- It was like, okay I'll give it to them.

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:12.373
- [Liu] Right.

00:12:13.690 --> 00:12:16.118
- My only regret is I still don't know

00:12:16.118 --> 00:12:18.583
if you're a fruit or a vegetable.

00:12:18.583 --> 00:12:20.833
(laughing)

00:12:22.310 --> 00:12:24.250
- Yep, all right, same kind of genre.

00:12:24.250 --> 00:12:29.250
Okay, for current actual
Marvel, DC, whatever.

00:12:29.271 --> 00:12:31.816
- Actual, for-real superhero.

00:12:31.816 --> 00:12:35.440
- For current universe superhero things,

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:40.220
the least cringe worthy
sci-fi superhero movie

00:12:40.220 --> 00:12:43.760
that I've actually seen is Doctor Strange.

00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:44.837
- Doctor Strange!
- Ooh.

00:12:44.837 --> 00:12:48.460
- And the reason that doesn't cringe me,

00:12:48.460 --> 00:12:49.860
is that a verb, to cringe?

00:12:49.860 --> 00:12:50.760
- You just made it one.

00:12:50.760 --> 00:12:51.593
- No, an active verb.

00:12:51.593 --> 00:12:53.870
I mean, I cringe, but to cringe somebody.

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:54.790
- You made it an active verb.

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:55.790
Okay, all right.

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:58.190
The reason it doesn't is
because it's all magic,

00:12:58.190 --> 00:13:01.500
because the premise of the
movie is that none of this

00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:04.054
is science anyways, or as say--

00:13:04.054 --> 00:13:05.020
- Yeah, supernatural.

00:13:05.020 --> 00:13:06.850
- Right, as Reed Richards would say,

00:13:06.850 --> 00:13:09.799
on his Fantastic Four comic series,

00:13:09.799 --> 00:13:12.446
he regularly would say--

00:13:12.446 --> 00:13:14.880
(Neil mumbles) The comic series.

00:13:14.880 --> 00:13:16.114
- Well that is the only real series.

00:13:16.114 --> 00:13:17.330
- [Tyson] Okay, fine.

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:18.503
- This cinematic universe stuff,

00:13:18.503 --> 00:13:20.617
that's all well and good.
- Its icing on a cake

00:13:20.617 --> 00:13:22.082
that was baked in the comic strips.

00:13:22.082 --> 00:13:22.915
- That's right,
- Okay.

00:13:22.915 --> 00:13:25.890
- We know what the canon
actually comes from.

00:13:25.890 --> 00:13:28.400
Yes, he acknowledges, he's
like the greatest scientist

00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:30.700
in the world, but he says, "I acknowledge

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:34.737
that magic is a science
I do not yet understand."

00:13:34.737 --> 00:13:35.572
- [Tyson] He did say that, yes?

00:13:35.572 --> 00:13:36.405
- That's right.

00:13:36.405 --> 00:13:37.380
And so, as a result--

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:38.765
- So did Princess Bubblegum, by the way.

00:13:38.765 --> 00:13:40.080
I'm sorry.
- Really?

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:40.913
- Yeah.

00:13:40.913 --> 00:13:41.880
- In what movie was that?

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:44.253
Well, its not a movie, its
series called Adventure Time.

00:13:44.253 --> 00:13:45.700
- Oh, yes!

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:47.540
- Is that the one where
they don't have elbows?

00:13:47.540 --> 00:13:48.590
- Yeah, that's Adventure Time!

00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:51.095
They have, like, noodle arms.

00:13:51.095 --> 00:13:52.118
- Noodle arms! (laughing)

00:13:52.118 --> 00:13:54.577
- Yeah, like noodle arms, yeah.

00:13:54.577 --> 00:13:55.913
All she says is basically,

00:13:55.913 --> 00:13:59.743
magic is just science unexplained.

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:01.700
Science we don't understand.

00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:03.690
- Okay, so Arthur C. Clark said, right?

00:14:03.690 --> 00:14:04.523
- Yes.

00:14:04.523 --> 00:14:06.560
- [Both] Any sufficiently
advanced technology

00:14:06.560 --> 00:14:07.697
is indistinguishable from

00:14:07.697 --> 00:14:08.810
- Magic.
- Science.

00:14:08.810 --> 00:14:09.960
Oh, from magic.

00:14:09.960 --> 00:14:11.040
- Oh no, from science, no.

00:14:11.040 --> 00:14:14.480
- Any sufficiently advanced technology

00:14:14.480 --> 00:14:15.480
- [Both] Is indistinguishable

00:14:15.480 --> 00:14:16.400
from magic
- From magic.

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:17.233
Yes.
- Magic.

00:14:17.233 --> 00:14:19.290
- Now, I don't mean to boast.

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:20.770
Okay, you can line up
for autographs later.

00:14:20.770 --> 00:14:21.603
- [Liu] Okay.
(laughing)

00:14:21.603 --> 00:14:25.616
- But I have a cameo in Sharknado 6

00:14:25.616 --> 00:14:26.610
- Excellent!

00:14:26.610 --> 00:14:28.575
and I play Merlin.
- Do you get eaten?

00:14:28.575 --> 00:14:29.830
Oh wait, I can't tell you. (mumbles)

00:14:29.830 --> 00:14:31.053
- I play Merlin.

00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:36.467
The plot line takes you
back to Medieval times.

00:14:36.467 --> 00:14:38.010
And I play Merlin.

00:14:38.010 --> 00:14:41.180
There's a time warp that
opens in the vortex.

00:14:41.180 --> 00:14:42.013
- [Liu] Of course there is!

00:14:42.013 --> 00:14:44.130
- Okay, (laughs) and the sharks,

00:14:44.130 --> 00:14:47.400
as they go through the vortex,
they end up crossbreeding

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:49.250
in this vortex with dragons.

00:14:49.250 --> 00:14:51.430
And so you have shark
dragon tornados back then.

00:14:51.430 --> 00:14:52.263
- [Liu] Wow.

00:14:52.263 --> 00:14:55.440
- Shark-dragonnados, and I play Merlin

00:14:55.440 --> 00:14:58.655
performing actual science
that everyone thinks is magic.

00:14:58.655 --> 00:15:00.621
- Because you're still a scientist.

00:15:00.621 --> 00:15:01.454
- Yeah, because I'm a scientist,

00:15:01.454 --> 00:15:03.750
and I was true to my roots.

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:06.473
- Now you do realize that you
can say no to these projects.

00:15:06.473 --> 00:15:09.140
(loud laughter)

00:15:13.490 --> 00:15:14.323
- Okay, Mom.

00:15:16.309 --> 00:15:18.650
Are we going to bring
this segment to a close?

00:15:18.650 --> 00:15:19.483
That was great question.

00:15:19.483 --> 00:15:20.316
- [Liu] Yeah, great question.

00:15:20.316 --> 00:15:21.149
- We had fun with that one.

