it doesn't fall out.

00:43:48.010 --> 00:43:49.117
- Right, that's one-G?

00:43:49.117 --> 00:43:49.950
- No, it could be zero-G.

00:43:49.950 --> 00:43:51.917
It could be weightless up there
because that would be one-G.

00:43:51.917 --> 00:43:53.040
- That's right, it could be.
- That's right.

00:43:53.040 --> 00:43:54.720
So, I take that back, sorry,

00:43:54.720 --> 00:43:56.170
bad example.
- No, you're right.

00:43:56.170 --> 00:43:57.576
- But I'm just saying--

00:43:57.576 --> 00:43:58.880
- Because that's what
happens on a rollercoaster

00:43:58.880 --> 00:43:59.750
where you go.

00:43:59.750 --> 00:44:02.620
- Yeah, you're weightless at the top.

00:44:02.620 --> 00:44:05.046
- The relevant formula is that
centripetal acceleration--

00:44:05.046 --> 00:44:07.485
- No, wait a minute, this would work.

00:44:07.485 --> 00:44:08.610
- [Liu] Its V squared over R.

00:44:08.610 --> 00:44:09.443
- No, no, no, watch.

00:44:09.443 --> 00:44:13.200
This would work, because
if it is zero-G at the top,

00:44:13.200 --> 00:44:14.330
and it's not falling out.

00:44:14.330 --> 00:44:15.163
- Right.

00:44:15.163 --> 00:44:17.450
That would be one-G,

00:44:17.450 --> 00:44:18.893
if I were in zero-G.

00:44:20.210 --> 00:44:21.374
- Sure.

00:44:21.374 --> 00:44:22.473
- All right, you lost me, man.

00:44:22.473 --> 00:44:23.306
(laughing)

00:44:23.306 --> 00:44:24.139
I'm sorry.

00:44:24.139 --> 00:44:26.965
- No, so the force up is now
counteracting the force down.

00:44:26.965 --> 00:44:29.810
Because we're doing
this experiment in one-G

00:44:29.810 --> 00:44:31.984
- Right, so the cancellation,
that is one-G in space.

00:44:31.984 --> 00:44:33.901
(drowns out Tyson's voice)

00:44:33.901 --> 00:44:34.734
- [Tyson] But in space, it
would be one-G in space.

00:44:34.734 --> 00:44:35.740
- One-G, okay.

00:44:35.740 --> 00:44:38.280
- So the point is, it's not
hard to figure out the speed.

00:44:38.280 --> 00:44:39.350
By the way, you wouldn't even need one-G.

00:44:39.350 --> 00:44:40.730
You can do 0.8-G.

00:44:40.730 --> 00:44:42.720
You can get ready for the
next planet you visit.

00:44:42.720 --> 00:44:43.920
Mars is 38%.

00:44:43.920 --> 00:44:46.130
- [Liu] 38% of our gravity.

00:44:46.130 --> 00:44:48.420
- So you can change the
rotation and get accustomed

00:44:48.420 --> 00:44:49.360
to being on Mars.

00:44:49.360 --> 00:44:51.608
It could be a very fun,
interesting exercise.

00:44:51.608 --> 00:44:54.490
- The equation is centripetal acceleration

00:44:54.490 --> 00:44:57.850
equals velocity squared divided
by the radius of rotation.

00:44:57.850 --> 00:44:58.683
- Okay.

00:44:58.683 --> 00:45:00.390
- So all you do is measure how far it is

00:45:00.390 --> 00:45:01.351
and you figure out how fast your spinning.

00:45:01.351 --> 00:45:02.184
- How fast you have to spin, that's it.

00:45:02.184 --> 00:45:03.370
- Jut push it and let it go.
- And by the way,

00:45:03.370 --> 00:45:07.788
I did the calculation for
the rotating section in 2001,

00:45:07.788 --> 00:45:09.230
- [Liu] Ahh!

00:45:09.230 --> 00:45:13.571
and they rotated that
three times too fast.

00:45:13.571 --> 00:45:14.404
- Really?

00:45:14.404 --> 00:45:15.237
- [Tyson] Yes.

00:45:15.237 --> 00:45:16.220
- So people were really bulking up?

00:45:16.220 --> 00:45:18.413
- No, no, no.
(laughing)

00:45:18.413 --> 00:45:20.936
- It was a heavy gravity spaceship.

00:45:20.936 --> 00:45:21.769
(laughing)
- They're just getting ready

00:45:21.769 --> 00:45:23.290
to get to Jupiter.

00:45:23.290 --> 00:45:25.100
- No, here's the thing.

00:45:25.100 --> 00:45:28.590
Okay, they surely knew what
speed it would have to be

00:45:28.590 --> 00:45:29.908
to be one-G.

00:45:29.908 --> 00:45:32.660
It was already rotating slowly.

00:45:32.660 --> 00:45:33.770
